{#
    Column headings for the folder lists, above the rows: sender, subject,
    attachments and date. A click on one sorts by it, and a second click on the
    same one reverses it.

    Only in the widest row shape. That is the only one with columns: below
    `row-line` (75rem of list width) the sender sits above the subject and there
    is nothing for a heading to stand over, so the strip is not drawn and the
    sort menu in the toolbar remains the way to change the order.

    Links, for the reason _sort_menu.html.twig gives: each is a GET into the
    same route inside #inbox-list-frame, and the controller remembers the choice
    as it answers. No JavaScript.

    The page is dropped, never carried, and the route's own parameters are kept
    (a label list lives at /mail/label/{id}) — both for the reasons given in the
    sort menu.

    The widths mirror the row's: its avatar and sender widths come from --avatar-size and --sender-col (Settings, List display), with a
    gap-3 between everything. The subject heading sits over the subject and the
    preview together, which share one flexible space and have no edge of their
    own to line up with.

    Parameters:
      current  ListSortOrder   the order in force
      route    string          the route each heading links to
#}
{% set base_params = app.request.attributes.get('_route_params')|default({})
    |merge(app.request.query.all)
    |merge({page: null})
    |filter(v => v is not null) %}

{% macro heading(column, current, route, base_params, extra) %}
    {% set next   = current.toggle(column) %}
    {% set active = current.column == column %}
    {% set label  = ('list.columns.' ~ column)|trans %}

    <a href="{{ path(route, base_params|merge({sort: next.value})) }}"
       data-turbo-frame="inbox-list-frame"
       data-turbo-action="advance"
       data-column-sort="{{ column }}"
       title="{{ 'list.columns.sort_by'|trans({'%column%': label}) }}"
       class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 min-w-0 rounded px-1 -mx-1 py-0.5 text-[11px] font-medium
              hover:bg-hover hover:text-ink transition-colors
              {{ active ? 'text-accent' : 'text-ink-faint' }} {{ extra }}">
        <span class="truncate">{{ label }}</span>
        {% if active %}
            <i class="fa-solid {{ current.isDescending ? 'fa-arrow-down' : 'fa-arrow-up' }} text-[9px]" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        {% endif %}
    </a>
{% endmacro %}

{% from _self import heading %}

<div data-column-headers
     role="row"
     class="hidden row-line:flex items-center gap-3 pl-3 pr-4 py-1 border-b border-line bg-surface">
    <span class="w-[var(--avatar-size,1.75rem)] shrink-0" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    <div class="w-[var(--sender-col,10rem)] shrink-0 min-w-0" role="columnheader" aria-sort="{{ current.column == 'sender' ? (current.isDescending ? 'descending' : 'ascending') : 'none' }}">
        {{ heading('sender', current, route, base_params, '') }}
    </div>

    <div class="flex-1 min-w-0" role="columnheader" aria-sort="{{ current.column == 'subject' ? (current.isDescending ? 'descending' : 'ascending') : 'none' }}">
        {{ heading('subject', current, route, base_params, '') }}
    </div>

    <div class="shrink-0" role="columnheader" aria-sort="{{ current.column == 'attachments' ? (current.isDescending ? 'descending' : 'ascending') : 'none' }}">
        {{ heading('attachments', current, route, base_params, '') }}
    </div>

    <div class="w-20 shrink-0 text-right" role="columnheader" aria-sort="{{ current.column == 'date' ? (current.isDescending ? 'descending' : 'ascending') : 'none' }}">
        {{ heading('date', current, route, base_params, 'justify-end') }}
    </div>
</div>
